.TH YUMED 8 "2026-08-01" "YUME 0.2.0-dev6" "YUME Manual"
.SH NAME
yumed \- YUME server daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yumed
[
.B --config
.I path
]
[
.I options
]
.PP
.B yumed
.B completion
.B bash
.PP
.B yumed
.B --help
.br
.B yumed
.B --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yumed
is the YUME server. It listens for authenticated YUME clients, validates
their auth keys, negotiates transport capabilities, and opens outbound
target sockets for allowed streams. It can also serve a real HTTP facade
for non-YUME requests, enforce operator-identity/no-log mode, manage authorized
keys, and expose relay/directory features when enabled.
.PP
For an accepted 2.0 tunnel, yumed is the public TLS/HTTP/2 endpoint. A
separately supervised Node.js 24 process on loopback supplies the genuine
cover site and never receives tunnel records or secrets.
.SH BASIC SETUP
.PP
.nf
sudo yumed \
    --listen 443 \
    --cert /etc/yume/server.crt \
    --key /etc/yume/server.key \
    --auth-keys /etc/yume/authorized_keys \
    --obfs-secret-file /etc/yume/obfs.hex \
    --inner-psk-file /etc/yume/inner.hex \
    --real-backend loopback://127.0.0.1:3000
.fi
.PP
Port 443 requires root or
.BR cap_net_bind_service .
After binding, the daemon can drop privileges unless
.B --root
is used.
.SH CORE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--config " path
Read server configuration from a JSON file.
.TP
.B transport_profile
JSON-only exact authenticated transport identity. YUME 0.2.0-dev6 accepts only
.BR chrome151-node24-v1 ;
stale identifiers fail startup and cannot be negotiated or downgraded.
.TP
.BI "--listen " port
Listen port.
.TP
.BI "--cert " path
TLS certificate.
.TP
.BI "--key " path
TLS private key.
.TP
.BI "--auth-keys " path
Authorized composite client identities. Each identity is an Ed25519 public key
followed by an ML-DSA-87 public key.
.TP
.BI "--auth-keys-meta " path
Regular-key policy JSON. Supports individual/bulk type, decimal fair-share
weight, per-key session caps, and permissions.
.TP
.BI "--admin-keys " path
Distinct composite second-factor identities for admin sessions. This store has
no policy metadata and must be disjoint from both visitor stores.
.TP
.BI "--operator-keys " path
Physically separate composite Ed25519 + ML-DSA-87 operator/controller
identities. Operator keys cannot be bulk. Outbound admin eligibility requires
membership in this store plus a different identity from
.BR admin_keys ;
metadata alone cannot grant it.
.TP
.BI "--operator-keys-meta " path
Non-admin policy JSON for operator identities (for example alias, weight, and
ordinary relay permissions). It cannot grant admin or full control.
.TP
.BI "--threads " n
Worker thread count in the range 0..256. Use
.B 0
for automatic selection.
.TP
.BI "--max-sessions " n
Hard cap on all simultaneously tracked sessions. Default 256. Use 0 only to
explicitly disable the cap.
.TP
.BI "--bulk-key-max-sessions " n
Default authenticated-session cap for each regular key marked
.BR key_type=bulk .
Default 64; per-key metadata may override it.
.TP
.BI "--rekey-window " n
Concurrent directional epoch offers accepted from one session, and the ceiling
on this server's own sending window. Range
.BR 1 - 64 ,
default
.BR 8 .
Each prepared epoch adds one negotiated epoch byte budget per rekey round trip
on high-latency links; the value is advertised in the TLS-protected AUTH
challenge and bound into the signed transcript. It bounds how much ML-KEM work
a peer can request. Under the default Extreme mode the budget is 256 KiB, with
independent limits of 512 frames and 500 ms sender-active time. The JSON key
.B security_mode
selects Extreme, Normal, Soft, or a complete bounded Ultimate policy; see
.BR docs/SECURITY_MODES.md .
.TP
.BI "--accept-rate-limit " n
Maximum newly accepted TCP connections per second. Use 0 for unlimited.
.TP
.BI "--tls-handshake-timeout-ms " ms
Abort slow TLS handshakes after
.I ms
milliseconds.
.TP
.BI "--egress-mbps " n
Aggregate weighted fair server egress cap in Mbit/s. Set it at or below the
real link limit. Active identities split the cap using metadata
.B weight
values; every bulk-key session is a separate identity.
.TP
.BI "--reverse-port-min " port
Minimum port for reverse forwards.
.TP
.BI "--reverse-port-max " port
Maximum port for reverse forwards.
.TP
.BI "--dns-server " ip
Resolver for outbound opens.
.TP
.B --robots-deny
Serve
.B /robots.txt
as
.B Disallow: /
through the existing HTTP facade. Disabled by default.
.TP
.BI "--filter-list " spec
Load a source or egress filter list. The form is
.BI client|egress|both:allow|deny:path
where
.I path
is JSON,
.B vpn_db.bin ,
or a
.B .tar.xz
archive containing one of those files.
.TP
.BI "--filter-geolite " path
Country lookup archive, GeoLite2-Country
.B .mmdb ,
or compact YUME
.B geoip_country_ipv4.db .
Archives are extracted at startup; hot-path lookup is in-memory.
.TP
.BI "--filter-memory-mib " n
Approximate memory cap for loaded filter data. Use
.B 0
for unlimited.
.TP
.BI "--client-filter-mode " mode
Client source filter mode:
.B blacklist
or
.BR whitelist .
.TP
.BI "--egress-filter-mode " mode
Destination filter mode:
.B blacklist
or
.BR whitelist .
.TP
.BI "--packet-egress " tun
Enable packet-native egress over an operator-prepared Linux TUN/NAT
interface. Disabled by default.
The separately installed
.B yume-packet-quick
helper can prepare and later remove a scoped TUN/NAT/UFW setup after an
explicit dry run and administrator confirmation; yumed never invokes it.
.TP
.BI "--packet-tun-name " ifname
TUN device to attach for packet-native mode. Default:
.BR yume-pkt0 .
.TP
.BI "--packet-cidr " cidr
IPv4 pool assigned to packet-native clients. Default:
.BR 10.89.0.0/24 .
The .1 address is reserved for the TUN side.
.TP
.BI "--packet-mtu " n
Packet-native MTU. Default:
.BR 1420 .
.TP
.BI "--obfs-secret-file " path
Load the mandatory admission secret from a protected file containing exactly
64 lowercase hexadecimal characters encoding 32 random bytes, with no newline.
.TP
.BI "--inner-psk-file " path
Load the separate mandatory random inner PSK in the same strict format.
.TP
.BI "--real-backend " url
Use the required genuine Node cover at
.BI loopback:// IP-literal : port .
DNS names, redirects, and non-loopback targets are rejected.
.TP
.B --allow-local-ip
Allow private and loopback destinations when key policy permits it.
.TP
.B --control-full
Allow unrestricted server-side network control when compile-time and
key-policy gates also permit it.
.TP
.B --root
Keep root privileges.
.TP
.B --boring
Use minimal logs.
.TP
.B --timing
Emit precise timing diagnostics in a Debug or RelWithDebInfo developer build.
Release and MinSizeRel binaries compile these hooks out and warn that the
option is unavailable.
.SH SECURITY OPTIONS
.TP
.B --inner-required
Redundant compatibility spelling for the mandatory 2.0 inner channel. The
ML-KEM-1024 + X25519 + PSK suite and per-message AES-256-GCM keys cannot be
disabled or peer-selected. Authenticated bounded ratchet policies may widen
the hybrid epoch budget without changing those algorithms. There are no
flags to select an inner mode, a hop layer, or a transport Argon2 stage.
.SH HTTP FACADE AND OPERATOR IDENTITY OPTIONS
.TP
.B --real
Serve real HTTP for non-YUME requests on the same port.
.BI "--real-index " path
HTML file served for
.BR / .
.TP
.BI "--real-root " dir
Serve GET/HEAD static files under
.IR dir
as the masquerade cover (implies
.BR --real ).
Files are returned with the correct MIME type,
.BR Content-Length ,
.BR Last-Modified ,
an nginx-style
.BR ETag ,
and
.BR "Accept-Ranges: bytes" ;
.B /
and directory paths serve
.IR dir /index.html.
Path resolution rejects traversal, encoded-slash tricks, control bytes, and
symlinks that escape the root; misses and non-GET/HEAD methods return the
profile 404. The same root backs the HTTP/1.1 probe and the H2 decoy. Pair with
.B --hide-in-the-crowd nginx
for the closest header fit.
.TP
.BI "--real-secret " string
Hidden metadata secret used by YUME tooling.
.TP
.BI "--real-secret-file " path
Load or create a real-facade secret file.
.TP
.B --operator-identity
Publish an operator identity proof and minimize identifying log fields where
supported. The proof authenticates CA-authorized operator control; it cannot prove that
the host does not inspect or retain traffic.
.TP
.BI "--operator-proof-mode " mode
Proof policy:
.BR auto ,
.BR local ,
or
.BR fixcraft .
.TP
.BI "--operator-proof-api " url
External proof API URL, used by
.B fixcraft
proof mode.
.TP
.BI "--operator-proof-token " string
External proof API token.
.TP
.BI "--operator-ca-key " path
Operator CA private key.
.TP
.BI "--operator-ca-cert " path
Operator CA certificate.
.TP
.BI "--operator-delegated-key " path
Delegated server identity private key.
.TP
.BI "--operator-delegated-cert " path
CA-signed delegated server certificate. Its issuer should identify the
operator and its subject should identify the server name/alias.
.SH RELAY AND DIRECTORY OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--server-name " name
Display name for this server.
.TP
.BI "--server-id " 32hex
Stable server endpoint ID.
.TP
.B --relay-enable
Enable client relay features.
.TP
.B --relay-disable
Disable client relay features.
.TP
.B --directory-enable
Enable endpoint directory.
.TP
.B --directory-disable
Disable endpoint directory.
.TP
.B --federation-enable
Enable static federation mode.
.TP
.BI "--peer " json
Add a federation peer.
.TP
.B --attach-local
Attach to a local running
.B yumed
instance.
.SH APPLICATION CODEC OPTIONS
Application codecs are protocol-aware shims, not raw TCP forwards. The
server must allow a codec globally and the client key must list it in
.BR auth_keys.meta .
.TP
.BI "--codec-allow " name
Allow an application codec id or alias (for example
.BR monero-rpc ).
Repeat for multiple codecs.
.TP
.B --allow-monero-rpc
Legacy alias for
.BI "--codec-allow " monero-rpc .
.TP
.BI "--service-allow " name
Allow a native ABI named service stream. The connected key must also
list the service in
.B permissions.allow_services
and the embedding process must call
.BR yume_server_register_service (3).
.TP
.BI "--monero-rpc-backend " host:port
Loopback backend for Monero RPC reconstruction. Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1:18089 .
Only loopback literals are accepted.
.SH DISGUISE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--hide-in-the-crowd " profile
Serve synthetic HTTP responses for non-YUME HTTPS probes using a named
disguise profile. Templates use common CDN or static-site error-page shapes
but are not native server implementations.
.SH HOST CONTROLLER
.TP
.BI "--host-mode " mode
WAN host controller mode:
.BR off ,
.BR private ,
or
.BR relay .
.B private
serves routed backends and rejects YUME clients by default.
.B relay
adds YUME client tunnel support on the same listener.
.TP
.B --accept-yume-clients
Accept authenticated YUME clients (default when host mode is off or relay).
.TP
.B --no-yume-clients
Reject YUME AUTH and carrier paths; probes receive disguise responses only.
.TP
.BI "--client-deny-action " action
How client IP filter denials close sockets:
.BR close ,
.BR reset ,
or
.BR drop .
.TP
.BI "--exposure-check " hostname
Probe whether the hostname is reachable via direct TCP or sits behind a
Cloudflare HTTP proxy. Result is logged at startup and exposed in
.BR runtime.info .
.TP
.B host_mode
.B accept_yume_clients
.B client_deny_action
.B routes
.B listeners
.B exposure_check_hostname
Host-controller fields in
.BR yumed.json .
Route and listener backends currently support loopback TCP URIs only
.RI ( loopback://127.0.0.1:PORT
or
.IR loopback://[::1]:PORT ).
See
.BR HOST_CONTROLLER.md .
.SH FEDERATION AND CLUSTER OPTIONS
Federation links are mutual TLS 1.3 connections between
.BR yumed (8)
peers. Each peer keeps its own
.B authorized_keys
and
.BR auth_keys.meta .
.TP
.B --cluster-bootstrap
Mark this node as a cluster bootstrap that accepts incoming peer dials.
Implies
.BR --federation-enable .
.TP
.BI "--cluster-join " spec
Dial a peer using the short form
.BI [id@]host[:port]?psk_file=path&carrier_secret_file=path[&pin=sha256] .
Bracket IPv6 addresses as
.BR [2001:db8::1]:443 .
Both secret-file parameters are mandatory. Repeat for multiple peers.
.TP
.B --public-node
Internet-facing hardening preset. Rejects dangerous server flags, requires
.BR --auth-keys
and a nonempty
.BR --obfs-secret-file ,
a mandatory inner PSK file, and the loopback Node backend, and tightens session
limits.
.TP
.BI "--federation-identity " path
Composite identity (Ed25519 + ML-DSA-87 PEM bundle) presented when dialing
federation peers. The peer must enroll this identity in its
.B --auth-keys
with a
.B federation_peer_id
meta entry.
.TP
.BI "--federation-operator-ca " path
CA certificate peers must present for federated TLS.
.TP
.BI "--peer " json
Add a federation peer using raw JSON (power-user form). Each peer requires
.B psk_file
(the pairwise AUTH v2 PSK, identical on both nodes) and
.B carrier_secret_file
(the peer's admission secret, i.e. the value of its
.BR --obfs-secret-file ),
because YUME 2.0 federation dials pass the same H2-carrier admission as
clients.
.SH AUTH_KEYS.META FORMAT
.B auth_keys.meta
is JSON keyed by composite identity fingerprint (hex). Each entry may
include an
.BR alias ,
.BR key_type
(
.B individual
or
.BR bulk ),
decimal fair-share
.BR weight ,
optional
.BR max_sessions ,
and a
.B permissions
object. Individual keys default to one session. Bulk keys use the server bulk
default unless a lower per-key cap is supplied, and they cannot receive
privileged controller, exec, LAN/full-control, codec/service, or federation
policy. Omitted dangerous permissions default to deny; relay-side
chat/file/bytes default to allow for individual keys and deny for bulk keys.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
{
  "0d4f3a...fingerprint...": {
    "alias": "alice",
    "key_type": "individual",
    "weight": 1.5,
    "permissions": {
      "allow_exec": true,
      "allow_local_ip": true,
      "allow_codecs": ["monero-rpc"],
      "allow_services": ["example-service-v1"],
      "allow_chat": true,
      "allow_file": true,
      "allow_bytes": true
    }
  }
}
.fi
.PP
Outbound administrator eligibility requires the visitor identity to be in the
physically separate
.B operator_keys
store and a different proved identity to be in
.BR admin_keys .
Visitor metadata cannot grant inbound admin, outbound admin, or full control.
A public key present in both regular and operator stores is rejected.
.PP
Generate fingerprints with
.BI "yumed --auth-keys " path " --keys-list" .
See
.BR docs/PERMISSIONS.md
for the full field table.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YUME_DNS_SERVER
Override the resolver used for server-side outbound opens when
.B --dns-server
is not set.
.TP
.B YUME_ANONYM_LOCAL_SIGN
When set to
.BR 0 ,
disable local operator identity proof signing even if operator CA/delegated
keys are configured.
Set to
.B 1
to force local signing on platforms where it is off by default.
.TP
.B SUDO_UID
.BR /
.B SUDO_GID
When started under
.BR sudo ,
these are read after bind/listen so PQ key files can be
.BR chown (2)
ed before privilege drop.
.SH KEY MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B --keys-list
List authorized keys.
.TP
.BI "--keys-add " pub.pem
Add an authorized public key.
.TP
.BI "--keys-remove " id
Remove an authorized key by fingerprint or alias.
.TP
.BI "--keys-alias " id " " alias
Set or update a key alias.
.TP
.BI "--keys-gen " prefix
Generate a composite Ed25519 + ML-DSA-87 identity as
.IR prefix .key
and
.IR prefix .pub .
.TP
.B --keys-gen-add
Append the generated public key to
.BR auth_keys .
.TP
.B --ui
Open the interactive server manager.
.SH AUTHORIZATION MODEL
Dangerous server features are behind three gates:
.IP 1. 4
compile-time feature switches, such as
.BR YUME_FEATURE_LAN_BRIDGE ;
.IP 2. 4
runtime server flags, such as
.BR --allow-local-ip ;
.IP 3. 4
per-key metadata in
.BR auth_keys.meta .
.PP
A key without metadata can authenticate, but dangerous permissions default
to deny.
.PP
EXEC policy fields remain reserved, but this version has no command-execution
backend. Direct and relayed EXEC requests fail closed regardless of build flag,
server config, or key metadata.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start a basic server:
.nf
sudo yumed --listen 443 --cert /etc/yume/server.crt \
    --key /etc/yume/server.key --auth-keys /etc/yume/authorized_keys \
    --obfs-secret-file /etc/yume/obfs.hex \
    --inner-psk-file /etc/yume/inner.hex \
    --real-backend loopback://127.0.0.1:3000
.fi
.TP
Start the mandatory 2.0 carrier with the real loopback Node cover:
.nf
sudo yumed --listen 443 --cert server.crt --key server.key \
    --auth-keys authorized_keys \
    --obfs-secret-file /etc/yume/obfs.hex \
    --inner-psk-file /etc/yume/inner.hex \
    --real-backend loopback://127.0.0.1:3000
.fi
.TP
Block VPN-provider egress destinations using an operator-supplied archive:
.nf
sudo yumed --listen 443 --cert server.crt --key server.key \
    --auth-keys authorized_keys \
    --filter-list egress:deny:/etc/yume/vpn_db.tar.xz \
    --filter-geolite /etc/yume/GeoLiteCountry.tar.xz
.fi
.TP
Generate and add a client key:
.nf
yumed --auth-keys /etc/yume/authorized_keys --keys-gen /tmp/alice --keys-gen-add
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/yume/authorized_keys
Authorized client public keys.
.TP
.I /etc/yume/auth_keys.meta
Regular-key permissions, type, fair weight, and session cap metadata.
.TP
.I /etc/yume/operator_keys
Physically separate operator/controller public keys.
.TP
.I /etc/yume/operator_keys.meta
Explicit operator policy metadata.
.TP
.I /etc/yume/vpn_db.tar.xz
Optional private VPN-provider blocklist archive. This file is
operator-supplied and should not be committed to the YUME source tree.
.TP
.I /etc/yume/
Common system configuration directory.
.TP
.I config/yumed.json
Example local server configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/yume/
Installed documentation in packaged builds.
.SH INSTALLATION
From a build tree:
.PP
.nf
cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build build -j$(nproc)
sudo cmake --install build
.fi
.PP
Manual man-page install:
.PP
.nf
sudo install -Dm644 docs/man/yumed.8 /usr/local/share/man/man8/yumed.8
sudo mandb
.fi
.PP
Debian package builds produced by CPack install this page automatically.
